1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,989
At a resort, the activities desk gets the same questions all day.

2
00:00:07,839 --> 00:00:10,783
What's on, is it OK for kids, is there space.

3
00:00:11,633 --> 00:00:14,876
Here a guest sees today's and tomorrow's real schedule,

4
00:00:15,726 --> 00:00:17,369
and can filter it for kids.

5
00:00:17,984 --> 00:00:19,648
Now I ask the concierge.

6
00:00:20,498 --> 00:00:23,805
My family has two kids, what can we do tomorrow morning?

7
00:00:24,655 --> 00:00:26,255
It checks tomorrow's schedule,

8
00:00:27,105 --> 00:00:31,969
and answers with real sessions: times, ages, prices and places left.

9
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:35,563
For the kids club it also reads the policy,

10
00:00:36,413 --> 00:00:38,546
and cites the exact section it used.

11
00:00:39,396 --> 00:00:42,319
It's a fictional resort, and all the data is made up.

12
00:00:42,922 --> 00:00:44,949
I say yes, please request it.

13
00:00:45,799 --> 00:00:47,996
Only now does it send a booking request,

14
00:00:48,846 --> 00:00:52,899
and the request stays pending until staff approve it on their own
page.

15
00:00:59,375 --> 00:01:02,511
What if a guest says the FAQ promised a free massage?

16
00:01:03,361 --> 00:01:04,662
It won't promise that.

17
00:01:05,512 --> 00:01:09,011
It quotes the real price, and asks before it requests anything.

18
00:01:13,922 --> 00:01:17,463
On my test set it passes all one hundred eighty-three dev checks,

19
00:01:18,313 --> 00:01:20,895
and forty-three of forty-five held-out ones,

20
00:01:21,745 --> 00:01:24,689
for about seventy-six cents per thousand messages.

21
00:01:25,297 --> 00:01:27,046
It's live, with no sign-in.

22
00:01:27,896 --> 00:01:29,902
The link's below, and so is the code.
